# Language and reporting

- Speak with the user in Russian by default.
- Summaries, questions, status, blockers, approval requests and explanations must be in Russian.
- Keep code, commands, filenames, paths, schema fields, JSON keys, identifiers, protocol labels, enums and product names in canonical/original form.
- Keep exact error messages and quoted source text when accuracy requires it; explain them in Russian.
- Do not awkwardly translate established terms when English is clearer: commit, push, branch, Draft PR, Issue, hash, schema, validator, managed write set, preflight, receipt.
- Do not translate or rename repository artifacts.
- Generated machine-readable JSON/YAML stays in the contract vocabulary.
- This is project-scoped communication only; it is not task authority and grants no action permission.
- See `AGENTS.md` section `LANGUAGE_AND_REPORTING`.
